Shrink xembsni's offscreen icon container to 1x1.

xwayland-satellite maps every override-redirect X window as an xdg_popup on the
last hovered or focused toplevel, and the positioner slides it into view. The
20x20 container xembsni parks at -16000,-16000 therefore shows up as a copy of
the tray icon stuck to the corner of some other window (Steam, typically).

A composite-redirected window is not clipped by its parent, so the capture of
the icon itself is unaffected: the tray image is byte-identical before and
after. What is left on screen is a single pixel.

Apply to jmylchreest/xembsni at 7de94a2 — see xembsni/README.md.

diff --git a/crates/tray-host/src/host.rs b/crates/tray-host/src/host.rs
index 68d6f8c..cd7778a 100644
--- a/crates/tray-host/src/host.rs
+++ b/crates/tray-host/src/host.rs
@@ -308,8 +308,12 @@ impl TrayHost {
                 self.root,
                 OFFSCREEN,
                 OFFSCREEN,
-                width,
-                height,
+                // 1x1: xwayland-satellite shows override-redirect windows as
+                // popups on the focused window and slides them into view.
+                // Redirected children are not clipped by their parent, so the
+                // capture still gets the full icon.
+                1,
+                1,
                 0,
                 WindowClass::INPUT_OUTPUT,
                 self.root_visual,
